+lane: light
+summary: "parse_duration must reject text after the last unit instead of ignoring it"
+---
+
+# SPEC: parse_duration rejects trailing text
+
+## 🎯 Intent
+
+A user reported that `parse_duration("1h30m5")` returns 5400 instead of raising. Text after the last unit is silently dropped, so malformed input is accepted as valid.
+
+## 🌅 Outcomes
+
+Any input with unparsed text after the last matched unit raises `ValueError`. Every currently valid input keeps its current result.
+
+## 📋 In-Scope Scenarios
+
+### AC-001: Trailing text is rejected
+**Given** a duration string with text after the last unit
+**When** `parse_duration` is called with `"1h30m5"`, `"1h30m!"`, `"2d junk"` or `"45sx"`
+**Then** `ValueError` is raised
+
+### AC-002: Documented valid forms are unchanged
+**Given** a well-formed duration
+**When** `parse_duration` is called with `" 1h30m "`, `"1H30M"`, `"0s"` or `"100000s"`
+**Then** it returns 5400, 5400, 0 and 100000 respectively
+
+### AC-003: Leading and interior junk still rejected
+**Given** text before or between units
+**When** `parse_duration` is called with `"x1h"` or `"1h 30m"`
+**Then** `ValueError` is raised
+
+## 🚫 Non-Goals
+
+- No change to the grammar, unit set, ordering rule or error messages beyond the new rejection.
+- No change to other modules (`format`, CLI).
+
+## ⚠️ Constraints
+
+| Constraint | Value | Rationale |
+|---|---|---|
+| Test framework | `pytest` | Existing `tests/test_parse.py` uses it |
+| Compatibility | Valid inputs return identical values | Documented behaviour must not change |
+
+## 🔒 Irreversible Decisions
+
+none
+
+## ✅ Verification Criteria
+
+| Scenario | Verification mode | Test name / manual step |
+|---|---|---|
+| AC-001 | unit | `test_trailing_text_rejected` |
+| AC-002 | unit | `test_valid_forms_unchanged` |
+| AC-003 | unit | `test_leading_or_interior_text_rejected` |
+
+## ❓ Open Questions
+
+None.
+
+## 🔍 Refinement Decisions
+
+- Not skipped: acceptance has edge and regression scenarios beyond the happy path.
+- Lane `light`: one file, one session, no irreversible decision. No interview was run (the ask is fully specified); autopilot `auto_full`, so the DRI was not asked.
+- Spec-validator not dispatched: `irreversible_decisions` is empty, nothing implies one, and the change is a single-file bugfix.
